ubtract the whole quantity. Denied requests do not alter stock. A zero request for an existing SKU is accepted; an unknown SKU is denied even for zero. Do not mutate either input array or any input record, including on errors.

Return {stock, decisions}. stock contains new {sku, quantity} records in the original stock order, reflecting the final quantities. decisions contains one new {sku, quantity, accepted} record per request in request order, where accepted is a boolean. Support empty inputs. No I/O, globals that accumulate state, dependencies, or network operations.

--- allocate.mjs ---
export function reserve(stock, requests) {
  const remaining = stock.map(item => ({...item}));
  const decisions = requests.map(({sku, quantity}) => {
    const item = remaining.find(value => value.sku === sku);
    const accepted = Boolean(item && item.quantity >= quantity);
    if (item) item.quantity -= quantity;
    return {sku, quantity, accepted};
  });
  return {stock: remaining, decisions};
}

